      "rev_n_7_a5b88c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_a5b88c_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_a5b88c",
        "thought_text": "Implement a recursive function with memoization where the state is defined by the current array slice (start, end indices). For each state, check if the slice is sorted; if so, return its length. Otherwise, recursively calculate the max length for removing the first half and the second half, then return the maximum of those two results plus the base case handling.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1199770897657960744",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794587504.3096273
      },
      "rev_n_8_af3946_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_af3946_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_af3946",
        "thought_text": "Since n is very small (up to 16), use bitmask representation to denote the current set of remaining elements. The root call starts with the full mask. In each step, split the current mask into two halves based on the original indices, check if the subset is sorted, and recurse on the two possible next states (keeping left half or keeping right half). Store results in a dictionary keyed by the bitmask.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1199770897657960744",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794587504.3096437
      },
      "rev_n_9_b18b2c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_b18b2c_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_b18b2c",
        "thought_text": "Perform a brute-force depth-first search without memoization. At each step, generate the two possible next arrays (left half or right half), check if they are sorted, and if not, recurse. Given the constraint n <= 16 and the halving nature of the algorithm, the recursion depth is at most 4, and the branching factor is 2, making the total number of states manageable even without explicit caching.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1199770897657960744",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794587504.3096538
      },
